THE GATE WAS FIXED, and it is the one this branch most needed. CLAUDE.md names
`test_movie_recorder.py` as the gate to run when touching movie code. It
printed `SKIP: no python with pcbnew + wx found` and exited 0 -- on a machine
with KiCad and wx installed and working. THREE defects in the gate itself,
stacked behind one another, each of which reports every claim it guards as
checked:

  1. the interpreter list carried #647's defect, never propagated out of the
     engine: no KiCad >= 6 installs at the unversioned
     `C:\Program Files\KiCad\bin\python.exe` (it is `...\KiCad\10.0\bin\...`).
     It CALLS `kicad_exact_fill.kicad_python_candidates()` now, which handles
     the versioned layout and VERIFIES a candidate can import pcbnew;
  2. `os.execv` on Windows re-splits argv on spaces, so once the versioned path
     was found the re-exec ran `C:\Program` with `Files\KiCad\...` as an
     argument and died before the gate started. Subprocess-and-exit on nt;
  3. the fixture board `kicad_files/fanout_output.kicad_pcb` does not exist,
     and `fanout_output1` -- the obvious substitute -- is GENERATED and
     gitignored, so naming either by path is the same self-skip one step
     later. It builds the board through `fixture_boards.ensure()` now.

